The rule table data/polimorf-rules.bin is a converted representation of
PyStempel 2.0.0's PoliMorf table, not a word-to-stem dictionary. Its BSD
2-Clause copyright notice and terms are preserved in licenses/POLIMORF.txt.
Retain that entire notice with redistributed table data.

Reference fixture provenance (including SJP and NSA tokens) is recorded in
scripts/corpus-sources.json and tests/fixtures/manifest.json. PyStempel's
README identifies its SJP test dictionary as Apache-2.0; the original
licensing overview and README are preserved in licenses/PYSTEMPEL.txt and
licenses/PYSTEMPEL-README.rst. NSA tokens are extracted from the specified
public repository revision solely for compatibility testing; this is not
an assertion of a blanket license for that separate repository's content.

This port changes the runtime language, table representation and loading API.
It preserves the upstream stemming behavior, including unusual outputs and
exceptions. Source revision and SHA-256 hashes appear in data/upstream.json.
